# Every image builds from the repo root, so whatever the root holds would
# otherwise be sent to the engine as build context: the customer's workbooks and
# documents, the history, the secrets, the tests. An allowlist, because a
# denylist grows a hole with every folder added.
#
# What the three Dockerfiles copy, and nothing else: the backend packages and
# their locks, the page, the orchestration code location, the telemetry package
# all three share, and the version the api reads from pyproject.toml.
# tests/static/test_dockerignore.py holds this file to those COPY lines.
*
!backend/
!frontend/
!orchestration/
!telemetry/
!pyproject.toml

# Caches and litter inside what is copied.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store
**/.pytest_cache/
frontend/README.md
